{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310630,"nonce":"feMF2E+1jllgXqNBLpdqi86/sPw=","title":"`++`/`--` silently dropped the store for every compound target. Arrays FIXED 863a956b; Map and anonymous-structure targets still lose it. ...","message":"**`++`/`--` computed the new value and threw it away for compound targets.**\n`lower_unary` (`compiler/src/ir/mir/expr/operators.rs`) matches the target to\ndecide where to write; the arm for an index target was `_ =\u003e {}`.\n\nOracle (haxe 4.3.6) vs rayzor, repro `scratchpad/incr`:\n\n| target        | haxe | before   | after 863a956b |\n|---------------|------|----------|----------------|\n| `arr[1]++`    | 21   | 20       | **21**         |\n| `m[\"k\"]++`    | 6    | 5        | 5 (still open) |\n| `o.n++` (anon)| 101  | 100      | 100 (still open)|\n| `plain++`     | 8    | 8        | 8              |\n\nSilent: exits 0, prints the wrong number.\n\n\nThe read and the write must not both go through `lower_lvalue_read` /\n`lower_lvalue_write` (`ir/mir/field/lvalue.rs:25`, `:70`): each lowers the\nreceiver AND the index itself, so with the read already done, `a[i()]++` would\ncall `i()` three times. The 167-line index-store body was extracted to\n**`store_index_with_regs(obj_reg, idx_reg, object_ty, value)`** (same file), and\n`lower_unary` lowers receiver and index once and uses them for both halves.\nVerified: value 21, index function called **once**, `++a[0]`→`2 2`,\n`a[2]++`→`3 4`.\n\n\n**Do NOT simply widen the fast path to Maps.** I tried; it turns a dropped store\ninto a **SIGBUS (exit 138)**. `lower_index_access`\n(`ir/mir/field/access.rs:1082`) is ARRAY-ONLY by construction: it does\n`build_load(obj)` to get the data pointer then GEPs by the index. For a Map the\nreceiver is the struct and the key is usually a pointer, so it faults. The fast\npath is therefore guarded by `self.map_index_info(object.ty).is_none()`.\n\nTo fix Maps properly, the READ needs the map getter with pre-lowered registers:\n`map_index_info(obj_ty)` (`access.rs:1478`) returns `(get_fn, key_ir, value_ty)`\nand `map_index_set_info` (`:1466`) the setter — but the key coercion the write\npath performs (`lvalue.rs`, the `store_index_with_regs` body) has to be shared\nwith the read, not duplicated.\n\nAnonymous-structure fields (`o.n++`) are a separate gap: `lower_unary`'s `Field`\narm hand-rolls a GEP from `field_index_map` and only covers class instance\nfields, missing the anon/Dynamic/cstruct/global branches that\n`lower_lvalue_write`'s Field arm has.\n\n**Conformance did not move** (421 before and after). The corpus cases touching\nthis construct fail on other causes too — the value here is the miscompile, not\nthe score. See [[feedback-perf-measurement-protocol]] for why that is still\nworth landing.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_increment_store_back_targets` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}